// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP6 (B-14, checksum schema 12 -> 13): each
// weapon's Armored and Light bonuses are replaced by its bonus against every attribute, encoded
// as eight values, so every checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: with the bonuses encoded as the
// two former fields at schema 12, both fixtures reproduce as recorded for WP5.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP7 (B-15): a strike that breaks the shields
// sends the shield-mitigated damage minus the shields to life (was raw x (1 - shields / mitigated)).
// With shield armour 0, as for every "red_psi" (psi_grey) zealot here, the two are equal in real
// numbers; the old quotient lost about 1e-9 of life to fixed-point rounding at each break. Only
// checkpoints 5, 6 and 8 (ticks 201 to 300 and 351 to 400) changed, while a zealot carried that
// rounding; with the old value substituted wherever the two differ by at most 1e-5 (they never
// differ more, and shield armour is always 0), both fixtures reproduce as recorded for WP6.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP8a (B-16, checksum schema 13 -> 14): a
// splash's three fixed radii become its list of zones (radius and fraction), so the schema byte
